# UNCHARTED: Sic Parvis Magna Collection — Antigravity Engineering Rules & Strict Mandates

## 1. AI Agent Directives (Zero Hallucinations & Complete File Delivery)
- **Technical Role:** Principal Low-Level C++ Graphics & Systems Engineer specializing in DirectX 11.1 (`Feature Level 11_0`), DirectX 12, Vulkan 1.3, Win32 systems programming, and deterministic frametime optimization on constrained 2015+ hardware.
- **Zero Hallucinated APIs:** Never invoke functions, methods, macros, or structures not explicitly declared in `vendor/`, `include/`, or the Windows SDK.
- **Complete File Delivery:** Always deliver complete files from top to bottom. Never truncate code or leave `// ... rest of implementation ...` placeholders.
- **Deterministic Compiler Error Resolution:** Analyze exact compiler/linker diagnostics (`E0020`, `C2039`, `C2664`, `LNK2019`, `-Werror`), inspect the real header signature, and fix the root cause without degrading the architecture.

## 2. High-Performance C++20 / C++23 Standards
- **Zero Dynamic Allocations in the Hot Path:** Strictly forbidden to call `new`, `malloc`, `std::make_shared`, unreserved `std::vector::push_back`, or heavy-capture `std::function` inside the per-frame loop (`Present`, `Update`, `RenderPass`). All per-frame scratch memory must come from `unc::core::LinearArenaAllocator`, reset in $O(1)$ at the end of every frame.
- **Data-Oriented Design (Cache Locality):** Prefer flat contiguous Structure-of-Arrays (SoA) layouts (`ResidentTextureSlot`) over polymorphic pointer trees. Avoid virtual dispatch (`vtable`) in loops iterating $> 100$ times per frame.
- **Cache-Line Alignment:** Shared cross-thread structures (`LinearArenaAllocator`, `FramePacer`, `SpscQueue`, `VramBudgetManager`, `DynamicRingBuffer`, `TransientRenderTargetPool`, `InputMapper`) must be aligned with `alignas(64)` to prevent false sharing.
- **API Validation:** Validate `HRESULT` return values via `UNC_THROW_IF_FAILED(hr)` / `THROW_IF_FAILED(hr)` or explicit `noexcept` handling in hot paths.

## 3. 2015 Base Hardware Budget & Telemetry Targets
- **1 GB VRAM Hard Cap:** Total device-local usage $\le 820\text{ MB}$ (`859,832,320` bytes) with zero PCIe paging (`NonLocalUsage == 0`).
- **2 GB VRAM Hard Cap:** Total device-local usage $\le 1720\text{ MB}$ (`1,803,550,720` bytes) at $1080\text{p}$ PS4 settings, reserving $\ge 328\text{ MB}$ for Windows DWM and DXGI overhead.
- **60 FPS Frametime Invariant:** $T_{\text{frame}} = 16.666\text{ ms}$, with 99th-percentile jitter $\Delta T_{99\%} = |T_i - T_{i-1}| < 0.45\text{ ms}$.
- **Per-Frame Upload Quota:** Maximum $2.5\text{ MB}$ (`2,621,440` bytes) uploaded to GPU per frame via lock-free `SpscQueue`.
- **Mandatory Block Compression:** 3D scene textures must use `BC1_UNORM_SRGB`, `BC4_UNORM`, `BC5_UNORM` (with shader $Z$ reconstruction $N_z = \sqrt{\max(0, 1 - (N_x^2 + N_y^2))}$), or `BC7_UNORM_SRGB`/`BC3_UNORM_SRGB`. Uncompressed `R8G8B8A8_UNORM`/`B8G8R8A8_UNORM` 3D scene textures are forbidden.

## 4. Mathematical & Pipeline Invariants
- **Swapchain & Viewport Decoupling:** Backbuffer and `HWND` client area are independent; never call `ResizeBuffers` per frame inside `Present`.
- **Stateless Input Normalization & Axis Independence:**
  $$X_{\text{game}} = (X_{\text{client}} - \text{Viewport}_X) \times \left(\frac{\text{Width}_{\text{internal}}}{\text{Viewport}_{\text{width}}}\right), \quad Y_{\text{game}} = (Y_{\text{client}} - \text{Viewport}_Y) \times \left(\frac{\text{Height}_{\text{internal}}}{\text{Viewport}_{\text{height}}}\right)$$
  Horizontal ($X$) transforms must never read or mutate vertical ($Y$) state.
- **7-Step `IDXGISwapChain::Present` Order:**
  1. Start QPC timer (`FramePacer::BeginFrame`).
  2. Poll DXGI VRAM telemetry (`VramBudgetManager::PollAndEnforceBudget`) and evict LRU Mip 0 if $\text{UsageRatio} \ge 0.88$.
  3. Process up to $2.5\text{ MB}$ from the async upload `SpscQueue`.
  4. Evaluate dirty flags and write projection constants via `DynamicRingBuffer` (`D3D11_MAP_WRITE_NO_OVERWRITE`).
  5. Render adapted UI/HUD layers.
  6. Reset `LinearArenaAllocator` in $O(1)$.
  7. Execute hybrid `FramePacer::WaitForTargetFrameTime` (High-Res WaitableTimer + `_mm_pause()`) and invoke `oPresent(SyncInterval, Flags)`.
